## Programming Without an OS

### no_std Environment

```xiom
// No standard library — just the core language
#![no_std]

// Entry point (no main, no runtime)
#[no_mangle]
pub fn _start() -> ! {
  // Initialize hardware
  init_clock();
  init_uart();

  // Your program
  uart_write("Hello from bare metal!");

  // Embedded programs never return
  loop {
    // Main loop
    process_sensors();
    update_actuators();
  }
}

// Define panic handler (required for no_std)
#[panic_handler]
fn panic(info: &PanicInfo) -> ! {
  // Blink LED, write to debug port, or reset
  loop {}
}
```

### Hardware Registers

```xiom
// Memory-mapped I/O for GPIO
const GPIO_BASE: usize = 0x40020000;
const GPIO_MODER: *mut u32 = (GPIO_BASE + 0x00) as *mut u32;
const GPIO_ODR: *mut u32 = (GPIO_BASE + 0x14) as *mut u32;

fn set_pin_output(pin: u32) {
  unsafe {
    let moder = GPIO_MODER.read_volatile();
    GPIO_MODER.write_volatile(moder | (1 << (pin * 2)));
  }
}

fn set_pin_high(pin: u32) {
  unsafe {
    let odr = GPIO_ODR.read_volatile();
    GPIO_ODR.write_volatile(odr | (1 << pin));
  }
}

fn delay(cycles: u32) {
  for _ in 0..cycles {
    unsafe { asm!("nop") };  // One CPU cycle
  }
}

fn blink_led() {
  set_pin_output(13);  // Onboard LED pin
  loop {
    set_pin_high(13);
    delay(1_000_000);
    set_pin_low(13);
    delay(1_000_000);
  }
}
```

### Interrupts

```xiom
// Timer interrupt handler
#[interrupt]
fn TIM2_IRQHandler() {
  // Clear interrupt flag
  TIM2_SR.write_volatile(0);

  // Toggle LED
  toggle_led();

  // Increment counter
  static mut COUNTER: u32 = 0;
  COUNTER = COUNTER + 1;
}

// UART receive interrupt
#[interrupt]
fn USART1_IRQHandler() {
  let byte = USART1_DR.read_volatile();
  rx_buffer.push(byte);
}
```

### RTOS Integration

```xiom
// FreeRTOS-style tasks
fn sensor_task() {
  loop {
    let temperature = read_temperature();
    if temperature > THRESHOLD {
      activate_fan();
    }
    os_delay(1000);  // 1 second
  }
}

fn communication_task() {
  loop {
    if let Some(msg) = rx_queue.receive(100) {
      process_message(msg);
    }
  }
}

fn main() {
  rtos::create_task(sensor_task, priority: 2, stack: 1024);
  rtos::create_task(communication_task, priority: 1, stack: 2048);
  rtos::start_scheduler();
}
```

### Constraints

| Constraint | Desktop | Embedded |
|-----------|---------|----------|
| RAM | GBs | KBs |
| Storage | TBs | MBs |
| CPU | GHz | MHz |
| OS | Full | None/RTOS |
| Heap | Yes | Often no |
| Stack | MBs | KBs |

